 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Mechanism:** a `contextvars.ContextVar` plus werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects.\n\n- **`src/tessel/globals.py:40`** defines `_app_var = ContextVar(\"tessel.app_ctx\")`. It holds the current `AppContext`.\n- **`src/tessel/globals.py:41-62`** defines the proxies. Each is a `LocalProxy` bound to `_app_var`, and each reads a different attribute of the current `AppContext`:\n  - `app_ctx` is the `AppContext` itself.\n  - `active_app` is `AppContext.app`, the `Tessel` instance.\n  - `g` is `AppContext.g`, an `_AppCtxGlobals`.\n  - `request` is `AppContext.request`, a `Request`.\n  - `session` is `AppContext.session`.\n- **`src/tessel/ctx.py:260`** defines `AppContext`. Its `__init__` stores `self.app = app` (line 307).\n  - `push()` calls `_app_var.set(self)` and keeps the token in `_cv_token` (lines 331 and 433).\n  - `pop()` calls `_app_var.reset(self._cv_token)` (line 498).\n  - Because the lookup is a `ContextVar`, each thread, greenlet or asyncio task sees its own current context.\n\nRequest and app contexts are merged into this single `AppContext`. `request_ctx` is a deprecated alias for `app_ctx` (`globals.py:65-75`).\n\nWhen no context is pushed, `_app_var` is unset and the proxy raises a RuntimeError. The message is `_no_app_msg` for `active_app` and `g`, and `_no_req_msg` for `request` and `session`. `ctx.py` uses `_app_var.get(None)` to test for a context (lines 112, 139, 232 and 257). `has_request` is the check for a request context.",
